    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Conduct a systematic capacity scan to test the logarithmic scaling hypothesis for $N_c(w)$ (minimum width for zero violation). Generate synthetic constraint data using smooth functions (e.g., low-degree polynomials or trigonometric sums) with varying sample sizes $w \\in [10^2, 10^4]$, train small MLPs of increasing hidden width $N \\in [10, 500]$, and measure the max absolute error on held-out constraints. Determine $N_c(w)$ as the smallest width achieving max error $\\leq 10^{-3}$. Plot $\\log N_c$ vs $\\log w$ to verify slope near 0 (logarithmic growth) and $N_c$ vs $\\ln w$ for linearity. Include bootstrapped confidence intervals for slope estimation and statistical significance testing."
    },
